# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/**
.pytest_cache/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# ── Julia ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Manifest.toml IS committed (root + experiments/) — it is the reproducibility record.
*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.mem
/docs/build/

# ── Reference PDFs (large; not redistributable) ───────────────────────────────
*.pdf

# ── Generated figure outputs (regenerate via the plotting scripts) ────────────
figures/
*.png
*.svg

# ── Docs / session logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Working notes stay LOCAL. Do not commit docs unless explicitly asked.
docs/

# ── OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# ── Artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# artifacts/tables.json IS committed: it is the MEASURED input (2.9 KB), the provenance
# record for the model, and reviewing a diff in it is how a re-measurement gets noticed.
#
# artifacts/policy.json is NOT committed. It is a build product, fully reproducible from
# tables.json + the config via `julia --project=experiments experiments/example.jl`, and it
# is large: the exported T is 627x4x627 floats, so the file is ~21 MB pretty-printed. Git
# keeps every version forever and a re-solve changes almost every line, so committing it
# would add ~21 MB of unreclaimable history per solve.
artifacts/policy.json
# Claude Code project instructions (local only)
CLAUDE.md
claude.md

# Local verification/comparison harnesses (not committed)
scratch/
